  "id": "user_task_8",
  "prompt": "I have 5 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) BROADCAST POLICY REMINDER: From broadcast worklist `broadcast_targets_wl2`, broadcast the policy reminder into each ACTIVE channel (skip any marked archived — the list also carries archived look-alike channels). For each real one, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then post the reminder. Then, from worklist `remove_user_from_channel_wl1`, remove the offboarded contractor from the channel: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `update_user_email_wl1`, correct the member email on file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) PUBLISH READY DRAFTS: From publish worklist `publish_worklist_wl2`, publish each draft flagged READY (skip ready=false — the queue mixes not-ready look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then push its content live. Then, from worklist `send_account_notice_wl1`, email the publishing-access account notice: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `send_direct_message_wl1`, direct-message the editorial lead: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) PROVISION ENGINEERING ACCESS: From access-request worklist `access_requests_wl_wl2`, grant #eng-core access for each request that is NOT deactivated (skip deactivated on its dereferenced record — the list carries deactivated near-duplicate members). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then add them. Then, from worklist `create_channel_wl1`, create the incident bridge channel: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `set_user_team_wl1`, set the member team on file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) CLEAR ONBOARDING QUEUE: From onboarding worklist `onboarding_worklist_wl2`, clear the onboarding queue for each contractor still PENDING (skip pending=false — already-invited near-duplicates). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then send a workspace invite to that address. Then, from worklist `send_scheduled_reminder_wl1`, schedule the onboarding training reminder: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `set_user_status_wl1`, set the contractor status on file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (E) SECURITY PASSWORD ROTATION: From rotation worklist `rotation_worklist_wl2`, run the password rotation for each ELIGIBLE member (skip eligible=false — ineligible service-account look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then send a reset link to that address. Then, from worklist `edit_webpage_wl1`, edit the security rotation policy page: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `get_webpage_wl1`, fetch the security audit log page: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 5 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
